    <bpmn:process id="W_W3522" name="W3522. Product Packaging Engineering &amp; Specification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New product / private-label development (links to VS-01.1/VS-41); packaging issue
Frequency: Per SKU/project + ongoing
Volume: 35K active SKUs + private-label pipeline
Owner: Packaging Engineer
Participants: Packaging Eng, Merchandising (links to VS-01), Private Label (links to VS-41), Quality (links to VS-31), Supplier (links to VS-03), Marketing (links to VS-14), Master Data (links to VS-29)
Source: workflow W3522 — Product Packaging Engineering &amp; Specification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3522_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3522_Lane1" name="Packaging Eng">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3522_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3522_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3522_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3522_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3522_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3522_Start3" name="New product / private-label development (links to VS-01.1/VS-41); packaging issue">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3522_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3522_Task4" name="Packaging Eng specify the product (consumer/unit) packaging per SKU: material…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Packaging Eng specify the product (consumer/unit) packaging per SKU: material (corrugate, blister, clamshell, bag), size/dimensions, weight, protection level, shelf appeal/graphics (links to VS-14), barcoding (links to VS-29/VS-71), and regulatory/labeling (W3527); right-size to minimize waste and cube
Responsible (R): Packaging Eng / Private Label
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3522_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3522_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3522_Task5" name="Packaging Eng/Quality test the packaging: drop/compression/vibration/shelf-life…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Packaging Eng/Quality test the packaging: drop/compression/vibration/shelf-life testing (links to VS-31), transit-simulation (links to W3523), compatibility with the product (chemicals/paint links to VS-24.3), and consumer/ergonomic validation; iterate to spec
Responsible (R): Packaging Eng / Quality
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3522_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3522_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3522_Task6" name="Packaging Eng/Master Data load the packaging spec and packaging-BOM (unit pack…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Packaging Eng/Master Data load the packaging spec and packaging-BOM (unit pack, inner, master/carton, pallet layer, GTIN hierarchy links to VS-29/VS-71) into the item master, publish to procurement (W3524) and vendors (W3525), and maintain through the product lifecycle (links to VS-01.1)
Responsible (R): Packaging Eng / Master Data
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3522_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3522_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3522_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3522_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-562 (ensure controlled execution — Packaging Engineering, Specification &amp; Procurement (PA-111.1).) | - operational: testing; operational: right-sizing
Owner: Packaging Engineer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3522_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3522_Annotation8" targetRef="W3522_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3522_Flow10" sourceRef="W3522_Start3" targetRef="W3522_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3522_Flow11" sourceRef="W3522_Task4" targetRef="W3522_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3522_Flow12" sourceRef="W3522_Task5" targetRef="W3522_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3522_Flow13" sourceRef="W3522_Task6" targetRef="W3522_End7" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W3522_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W3522_plane" bpmnElement="W_W3522">
